  "lineage": "Nepali lok geet (\"folk songs\") encompass the broad popular-and-traditional song repertoire of Nepal, including regional variants from the Newari, Tharu, Gurung, Magar, Tamang, Rai, Limbu, and other ethnic communities, plus the urban Kathmandu Valley pan-Nepali pop synthesis. The genre developed through the twentieth-century Radio Nepal (founded 1951) commercial-recording era. Standard instrumentation centers on madal two-headed barrel-drum, tabla, sarangi (Nepali, four-string short-neck bowed lute distinct from Hindustani sarangi), and bansuri flute. Repertoire spans selo (Tamang call-and-response), tappa (regional ballad), and roila (Karnali region).",
